.\" Snippet, not a page: no .TH or .SH here. Manpage opens .SH EXAMPLES itself.
Evaluate an expression without writing a file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pynix eval --expr '1 + 1'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Build the hello package of the flake in the current directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pynix build --flake .#hello
.RE
.fi
.PP
Open a development shell for that package and run make inside it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pynix develop --flake .#hello -- make -j4
.RE
.fi
.PP
List the roots that keep store paths alive:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pynix store gc print-roots
.RE
.fi
